/*
 * I SPOON — full firmware
 *
 *   Touch + animated splash + temperature display
 * + BMI323 bite counter (BLE binary packets)
 * + nPM1304 battery monitor (10-bit ADC over I2C)
 * + Top status bar:  [BT-icon]  [battery%]
 *
 *   2 s touch hold  -> wake panel, "I SPOON" splash, then live temp view.
 *                      BLE starts advertising. PMIC keeps charging if USB.
 *   3 s touch hold  -> sleep panel, stop BLE, disconnect, reset bite count.
 *
 * Top bar (only visible in UI_TEMP):
 *   - Battery percent as text in the top-right corner (e.g. "85%")
 *   - Bluetooth icon to the left of it, ONLY when a phone is connected
 *
 * Target: nRF52840, NCS v3.1.x.
 *
 * BLE binary packet format (little-endian):
 *   [type:1] [seq:2] [ts_ms:4] [payload]
 *
 * Types:
 *   0x01 IMU    : 6 x int16  (ax,ay,az,gx,gy,gz raw LSB)        -> 19 B
 *   0x02 STATE  : uint8 state_id                                ->  8 B
 *   0x03 BITE   : uint16 count + 3 x int16 rot*10 deg           -> 15 B
 *   0x04 RECAL  : float32 baseline (g)                          -> 11 B
 *   0x05 INFO   : uint8 info_code                               ->  8 B
 *   0x06 BATT   : uint16 mV + uint8 percent + uint8 flags       -> 12 B
 *   0x07 TEMP   : int8 Celsius                                  ->  8 B
 */

